{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Yiskah.</b> Rashi explained: this is Sarah. For Haran fathered Sarah six years earlier, according to the reckoning of their ages; and so it is stated explicitly in Bereshit Rabbah. And we find in the chapter 'Ben Sorer uMoreh': the early generations — each and every one — father at eighteen years; and likewise Betzalel, and Bat Sheva, and Er and Onan."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The comment names Rashi explicitly; in keeping with the compiler's voice the name is rendered as it appears in the text. 'Six years earlier' translates לשש שנים לפי חשבון שמותם, i.e., six years before the standard age of fathering."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:53.405717988Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}